From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XeresRazor <shinohara@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:00:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mina the Hollower 1.0.6 (v327680): register the build and its
 arena cuts

Update 1.0.6's main (e86ae07b...) has the same two TLSF arenas as 1.0.5's,
"Default Mem" and "Render Mem", 0x20 further on (main+0x6d8cc and +0x6dc2c).
Without registering it, the engine's own cuts do not reach it and a build for an
iPhone-sized alias region stops at the address region check.

- game.tsv: a build row for v327680 (1.0.6, main e86ae07b..., the same sdk)
- patches.py: the same two cuts as 1.0.5 (1 GB and 256 MB), so the region check
  gives the same stdalloc_cap (0xa4000000) and the profile keeps it
- the game note and the games table say both updates are registered

1.0.6 has 90 of its 110 shader keys different from 1.0.5's, so the profile's
tables (made from 1.0.5) do not hold them: a 1.0.6 build is packed from a
derived profile with its own tables, as designed. Registering both versions'
tables needs both updates in one folder (shader_versions).

Checked on the Mac from a folder with only 1.0.6: the region check passes with
1.0.5's numbers, and a 120 s headless run on the 4.375 GB alias region with the
Mac shader libraries gave no [RED] line and 6,900 frames at 60 fps. Play past the
title is not covered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Mina the Hollower 1.0.6: register the build and its arena cuts, which the 1.0.5-keyed profile of seedds/nxnative#1021 does not reach
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1273

